WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:03.270
- [Instructor] We are told a
rectangle has a height of five

00:03.270 --> 00:08.220
and a width of 3x
squared minus x plus two.

00:08.220 --> 00:10.460
Then we're told express the area

00:10.460 --> 00:12.550
of the entire rectangle,

00:12.550 --> 00:14.930
and the expression should be expanded.

00:14.930 --> 00:18.900
So pause this video and see if
you could work through this.

00:18.900 --> 00:21.420
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:21.420 --> 00:23.390
What this diagram is showing us

00:23.390 --> 00:25.910
is exactly an indicative rectangle,

00:25.910 --> 00:28.440
where its height is five

00:28.440 --> 00:33.100
and its width is 3x
squared minus x plus two.

00:33.100 --> 00:35.410
What this shows us is is the area

00:35.410 --> 00:38.440
of the entire rectangle can be broken down

00:38.440 --> 00:40.820
into three smaller areas.

00:40.820 --> 00:44.200
You have this blue area right over here.

00:44.200 --> 00:46.860
Where the width is 3x
squared, the height is five,

00:46.860 --> 00:48.463
so what's that area going to be?

00:48.463 --> 00:50.900
It's going to be the height times width.

00:50.900 --> 00:53.780
Five times 3x squared.

00:53.780 --> 00:57.220
That's the same thing as 15x squared.

00:57.220 --> 01:00.880
Now what about this purple
area right over here?

01:00.880 --> 01:02.930
It's going to be height times width again,

01:02.930 --> 01:05.870
so it'll be five times negative x,

01:05.870 --> 01:08.580
which is the same thing as negative 5x.

01:08.580 --> 01:09.570
I know what some of you are thinking,

01:09.570 --> 01:12.690
how can you have a width of negative x?

01:12.690 --> 01:14.070
Well, we don't know what x is,

01:14.070 --> 01:16.270
so this is all a little bit abstract.

01:16.270 --> 01:19.610
But you could imagine having
x be a negative value,

01:19.610 --> 01:22.770
in which case this actually
would be a positive width.

01:22.770 --> 01:24.080
Another thing you might be saying is,

01:24.080 --> 01:26.420
hey, this magenta area,
when I just eyeball it,

01:26.420 --> 01:28.540
looks like it has a larger
width than this blue area.

01:28.540 --> 01:29.373
How do we know that?

01:29.373 --> 01:30.206
We don't.

01:30.206 --> 01:32.960
They're just showing this
as an indicative way.

01:32.960 --> 01:35.100
They might have actually the same width.

01:35.100 --> 01:37.310
They might have, one might
be larger than the other,

01:37.310 --> 01:38.490
but this is just showing us that

01:38.490 --> 01:39.980
they're not necessarily the same.

01:39.980 --> 01:41.100
It's very abstract.

01:41.100 --> 01:42.450
It's definitely not drawn to scale

01:42.450 --> 01:44.940
'cause we don't know what x is.

01:44.940 --> 01:47.020
All right, and then this last area

01:47.020 --> 01:49.160
is going to be the height, which is five,

01:49.160 --> 01:50.920
times the width, which is two.

01:50.920 --> 01:53.050
So that's just going to be equal to 10.

01:53.050 --> 01:56.000
So what we just saw is that
the area of the whole thing

01:56.000 --> 01:58.610
is equal to the sum of these areas,

01:58.610 --> 02:03.440
and the sum of those areas is 15x squared

02:03.440 --> 02:06.860
plus negative 5x, or we could
just write that as minus 5x.

02:06.860 --> 02:09.480
And then we have plus 10.

02:09.480 --> 02:11.010
Now I know what some of you are thinking.

02:11.010 --> 02:12.610
If I know that the height is five

02:12.610 --> 02:14.640
and the width is this value,

02:14.640 --> 02:16.920
well couldn't I have
just multiplied height

02:16.920 --> 02:21.020
times the entire width, 3x
squared minus x plus two,

02:21.020 --> 02:24.410
and then I would've just
naturally distributed the five?

02:24.410 --> 02:26.630
And essentially that's
exactly what we did here.

02:26.630 --> 02:27.890
Area models, you might have first

02:27.890 --> 02:29.340
seen them in elementary school,

02:29.340 --> 02:32.260
really to understand the
distributive property.

02:32.260 --> 02:35.740
So if you distribute the
five you get 15x squared

02:35.740 --> 02:38.010
minus 5x plus 10.

02:38.010 --> 02:39.110
Same idea.

02:39.110 --> 02:40.360
Let's do another example.

02:41.780 --> 02:43.570
So here we're given another rectangle.

02:43.570 --> 02:44.960
It has a height of 2x.

02:44.960 --> 02:46.360
We see that right there.

02:46.360 --> 02:48.150
A width of 3x plus four.

02:48.150 --> 02:50.020
We see that over there.

02:50.020 --> 02:53.280
Express the area of the entire rectangle.

02:53.280 --> 02:54.860
So same drill.

02:54.860 --> 02:56.050
See if you can pause this video

02:56.050 --> 02:57.603
and work on this on your own.

02:58.640 --> 02:59.500
All right.

02:59.500 --> 03:02.900
Well, we can see that the height is 2x,

03:02.900 --> 03:07.060
the width in total is 3x plus four.

03:07.060 --> 03:09.620
But we can clearly see that
the area of the entire thing

03:09.620 --> 03:11.560
can be broken up into this blue section

03:11.560 --> 03:13.050
and this magenta section.

03:13.050 --> 03:16.230
The blue section's area is 3x times 2x.

03:16.230 --> 03:20.620
So 3x times 2x, which
is equal to 6x squared.

03:20.620 --> 03:22.270
The magenta section is equal

03:22.270 --> 03:25.270
to width times height, its area.

03:25.270 --> 03:27.510
So that going to be equal to 8x.

03:27.510 --> 03:29.080
So the area of the whole thing is going

03:29.080 --> 03:30.250
to be the sum of these areas,

03:30.250 --> 03:32.990
which is going to be 6x squared plus 8x.

03:32.990 --> 03:33.920
And we're done.

03:33.920 --> 03:36.340
Once again, we could've
just thought about it as

03:36.340 --> 03:39.760
the height is 2x, we're gonna
multiply it times the width,

03:39.760 --> 03:41.520
times 3x plus four.

03:41.520 --> 03:44.000
Then we just distribute the 2x.

03:44.000 --> 03:46.669
So 2x times 3x is 6x squared.

03:46.669 --> 03:49.370
2x times four is 8x.

03:49.370 --> 03:51.010
Same idea.

03:51.010 --> 03:53.600
It's really just to
make sure we understand

03:53.600 --> 03:57.670
that when we distribute a 2x
onto this 3x and this four,

03:57.670 --> 04:00.750
we can conceptualize it as figuring out

04:00.750 --> 04:05.153
the areas of the sub-parts
of the entire rectangle.
